>
  <p>
    <strong>Garage management software is a system that brings a workshop's daily operations into one place:</strong>
    bookings, job cards, bay scheduling, vehicle history, inspections, parts, invoicing and customer reminders. UK
    systems also handle MOT reminders and DVLA or VRM vehicle lookups, since those are specific to how UK garages
    are regulated and how vehicles are identified.
  </p>

  <h2>What a garage runs without it</h2>
  <p>
    Most workshops start with a paper diary or a shared spreadsheet for bookings, a separate system for invoicing,
    and a WhatsApp group or a wall of sticky notes for job status. It works until the garage gets busy: bookings get
    double-booked, MOT reminders get missed, and nobody can say which of three vehicles in bay 2 is actually ready.
  </p>

  <h2>What to look for in garage management software</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><a href="/features/workshop-board">A live workshop board</a></strong> that shows every bay and every job without refreshing a spreadsheet.</li>
    <li><strong>VRM lookup</strong> so a registration number pulls vehicle details automatically, not manual entry.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/features/vehicle-inspections">Digital inspections</a></strong> customers can see and approve from their phone before work starts.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/features/mot-reminders">MOT and service reminders</a></strong> that go out without someone remembering to send them.</li>
    <li><strong>Invoicing that syncs to accounts</strong> — Xero or Sage — so nothing gets rekeyed by hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Coverage for the trades around a garage</strong> — <a href="/mobile-tyre-fitting-software">mobile tyres</a>, <a href="/auto-locksmith-software">locksmiths</a>, <a href="/ecu-remapping-software">ECU remapping</a> — not just
      the core bay work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How GarageCloud approaches this</h2>
  <p>
    GarageCloud connects {FEATURES.length} modules into one system: {FEATURES.map((f) => f.title).join(", ")}. The
    aim is a single login that covers what a workshop actually does day to day, rather than a core booking tool with
    everything else bolted on as an add-on.
  </p>

  <h2>Is garage management software worth it for a small workshop?</h2>
  <p>
    The case is usually time, not headcount: a single system removes the double-entry between a booking diary, an
    invoicing tool and an accounts package, and it stops MOT and service reminders depending on someone remembering
    to send them. For a one or two-bay independent garage, that is often the difference between chasing paperwork in
    the evening and not. See <a href="/pricing">GarageCloud pricing</a> for the plan that fits.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
